  {
    "episode_id": 88869,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/8/88869.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "We are getting to that point. I mean, the economic devastation that is going off and the high unemployment and the bankruptcies that are foreseeable on the future. If we don't get America back to work sooner rather than later, the devastation associated with that and the public health impact. So you remember when you go into a Great Depression, there are deaths, there are impacts on public health that are dire and the numbers on public health of the virus could pale in comparison to that type of situation. Now that's why we're working hard to avert it. So I'm glad to see we're going down the regional approach and we were able to convince the governor to get Western New York up and",
