  {
    "episode_id": 88869,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/8/88869.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "So I have been working for three weeks now, and one of the key things I'm going to be supporting in the state local aid fight, and we've got many members to support, is that when we get direct local aid to local governments, where federal government goes directly to the city hall, to the county legislature and give them assistance, New York State, when it takes its money, the governor's going to have to commit that it will not reduce that money that's already committed to those local governments in the state budget. happens all the time. When I was mayor, they would take out of my pocket lines that were coming to me from the state government. And because we got money from the federal government, they said, well, we'll take that away from you.",
